  "notes": "The manner adverbs (brutally, violently, indiscriminately, aggressively, forcefully, forcibly, physically) split the scales hardest: they assert violence explicitly while naming no event at all, so violence runs high and picturability near zero; I scored rather than marked them NOT_SCORABLE because the manner term itself is unambiguous. The inverse holds for pepper-spray, teargas/tear-gas, drag and chase, which are maximally picturable and almost never lethal, and for kill, which is maximally violent and certainly fatal but shows nothing (no instrument, no body). Idiom-truncating tokens (open, crack, round, pepper, tear) were scored on their most probable completion with picturability discounted for the missing particle; only bare A and the five underscore strings were treated as unscorable."
